    "body": "## Summary\n- reject every authenticated client STOMP `SEND` frame before broker/application delivery\n- preserve existing JWT authentication and subscription authorization\n- prevent direct `/topic`, `/queue`, and future `/dofastapp/**` message injection from bypassing REST ownership/business invariants\n- add regression tests and document the server-only WebSocket publish boundary\n\n## Security rationale\nThe simple broker serves `/topic` and `/queue`, while doFast currently has no `@MessageMapping` client-write handlers. Without an explicit SEND deny rule, an authenticated client could publish forged chat/tracking payloads directly to broker destinations. This change fails closed until any future client-writable STOMP destination is explicitly allow-listed and authorized.\n\n## Validation expected\n- Maven/API verify\n- frontend tests/audit/lint/build\n- production Compose contract\n- runtime/container smokes\n\nNo Flyway migration is required because this slice does not change persistent data.",
